{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014Sdh6DwFs43kh9kcKUxo8n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All acceptance criteria verified:\n\n- **AC1** `go build ./pkg/format/...` compiles with no errors\n- **AC2** `go vet ./pkg/format/...` reports no issues\n- **AC3** Binary (1024-based) size formatting: `HumanSize(0, {Binary:true})` → `\"0\"`, `HumanSize(1024, {Binary:true})` → `\"1.0K\"`, `HumanSize(1048576, {Binary:true})` → `\"1.0M\"`, suffixes go through `K/M/G/T/P/E` covering the exabyte range\n- **AC4** SI (1000-based) size formatting: `HumanSize(0, {})` → `\"0\"`, `HumanSize(1000, {})` → `\"1.0kB\"`, `HumanSize(1000000, {})` → `\"1.0MB\"`, suffixes go through `kB/MB/GB/TB`\n- **AC5** Color output produces valid ANSI SGR escape sequences for all 11 standard file types: directory (`\\033[34m`), symlink (`\\033[36m`), executable (`\\033[32m`), pipe (`\\033[33m`), socket (`\\033[35m`), block device (`\\033[33;1m`), char device (`\\033[33;1m`), setuid (`\\033[37;41m`), setgid (`\\033[30;43m`), sticky (`\\033[37;44m`), other-writable (`\\033[34;42m`)\n- **AC6** When `SetColorEnabled(false)` is called, `FileTypeColor` and `Reset` return empty strings with no ANSI escape sequences\n\n**Summary of implementation:**\n\n**`pkg/format/size.go`** (prd003-format R3): Implements `HumanSizeOpts` struct and `HumanSize` function. Binary mode uses base 1024 with suffixes `K/M/G/T/P/E`. SI mode uses base 1000 with suffixes `kB/MB/GB/TB`. Values below the base are returned as integers without suffix. Values at or above the base are formatted with one decimal place. Zero always returns `\"0\"`.\n\n**`pkg/format/color.go`** (prd003-format R2): Implements ANSI color constants matching GNU ls LS_COLORS defaults, `FileTypeColor` (checks permission-based overrides before file type), `Reset`, `ColorEnabled` (TTY detection via TIOCGWINSZ ioctl), `SetColorEnabled` (process-global override for `--color=always/never`), and `ResetColorEnabled` (revert to auto-detect). A three-state `colorMode` controls behavior: auto-detect, forced on, or forced off."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":68397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":293},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7bb5990-f84b-4cb6-be6f-4a1410105a37","uuid":"958816a6-5338-4722-9ef5-5f1d5ea9e66c"}
